1
00:00:00,978 --> 00:00:03,938
SHELDON: How's this?
"Pleased to meet you, Dr. Gablehauser.

2
00:00:04,106 --> 00:00:06,986
(Sheldon:)How fortunate for you
the university has chosen to hire you...

3
00:00:07,151 --> 00:00:10,241
...despite the fact you've done
no original research in 25 years...

4
00:00:10,404 --> 00:00:12,324
...and instead have written books...

5
00:00:12,490 --> 00:00:15,410
(Sheldon:)...that reduce the great concepts
of science to anecdotes...

6
00:00:15,576 --> 00:00:16,786
(Sheldon:)...each one dumbed down...

7
00:00:16,952 --> 00:00:20,702
(Sheldon:)...to accommodate the duration
of an average bowel movement."

8
00:00:21,457 --> 00:00:23,167
[SPEAKS IN HAWAI IAN]

9
00:00:26,170 --> 00:00:28,920
- "Mahalo" is a nice touch.
- Hmm.

10
00:00:29,340 --> 00:00:31,510
(Sheldon:)Only eight consonants
in the Hawaiian language.

11
00:00:31,675 --> 00:00:34,015
LEONARD:
Interesting, you should lead with that.

12
00:00:36,180 --> 00:00:38,850
(Raj:)Oh, God, look at this buffet.

13
00:00:39,016 --> 00:00:40,846
(Raj:)I love America.

14
00:00:41,018 --> 00:00:45,228
- You don't have buffets in India?
- Of course, but it's all Indian food.

15
00:00:45,564 --> 00:00:48,404
(Raj:)You can't find a bagel in Mumbai
to save your life.

16
00:00:48,567 --> 00:00:50,357
Smear me.

17
00:00:51,821 --> 00:00:54,861
- Well, here's an interesting turn of events.
- What?

18
00:00:57,576 --> 00:00:58,866
(Leonard:)Howard brought a date?

19
00:00:59,036 --> 00:01:04,026
(Sheldon:)A more plausible explanation is that his
work in robotics has made an amazing leap.

